  "question": {
    "text": "In the following reactions, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ZnO</mi></math>&nbsp;is respectively acting as a/an,<br /><br />(i) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ZnO</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Na</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi>Na</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>ZnO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math><br /><br />(ii) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ZnO</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi>ZnCO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "MWegR",
      "text": "base and base.",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "mRjVq",
      "text": "acid and acid.",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "I6y9b",
      "text": "acid and base.",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "8HKqy",
      "text": "base and acid.",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Amphoteric&nbsp;means it behaves as both acid and&nbsp;base.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Na</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>&nbsp;is basic oxide and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ZnO</mi></math>&nbsp;will act as acidic oxide in reacting with this oxide.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is acidic oxide and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ZnO</mi></math>&nbsp;will act as basic oxide in reacting with this oxide.&nbsp;So, with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Na</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>,&nbsp;it acts&nbsp;as an acid and with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>, it&nbsp;acts as a base.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
